 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? First, check your setting. Many recording apps have a simple echo button that adds badness. Then stand still and close to a solid wall. Come off the back of the house, so it reads the room as room, not a tube. Then an external microphone makes big difference. A cheap one plugs into your phone. Use it in your hand. About the length of your palm. It blocks your ear and gives you direct sound. Another room is fine. Use a desk as a barrier for the worst echo.",
